__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
/dist/
/build/
*.egg-info/

# secrets & scraped data - NEVER commit (CLAUDE.md §3)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# The portal's missing intermediate CA is a PUBLIC certificate and the manifests mount it as a
# ConfigMap, so it must be committed despite the *.pem rule above.
!deploy/base/portal-ca.pem
cookies.json
storage_state.json
# Anchored with a leading slash so they match only at the repository root. Unanchored,
# `state/` also matched src/tele_scraper/state/ and silently kept the dedup store out of the
# repository - the package imported fine locally and was simply absent in CI.
/debug/
/state/
*.sqlite3

# Real production values live here: credentials, recipient addresses and chat ids, none of
# which may be committed (CLAUDE.md §3.1, §3.2, §14.6). The committed prod overlay keeps
# placeholders; this one layers the real thing on top and never leaves the machine.
/deploy/overlays/prod-local/
